OL,3,GNEWSAWhy are 3,000 fridges piling up in
OL,4,ANorfolk?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThousands of fridges and freezers are
OL,7,Fbeing stored at a Norfolk recycling
OL,8,Fsite due to a national backlog of
OL,9,Fspecialist waste collections.
OL,11,FAround 3,000 appliances are being
OL,12,Fstored at Mayton Wood Recycling Centre
OL,13,Fnear Coltishall as a short-term
OL,14,Fsolution, but Norfolk County Council
OL,15,Fsaid it is nearly at full capacity.
OL,17,FThe Department for Environment, Food
OL,18,Fand Rural Affairs (Defra) said the
OL,19,Fnational situation is due to a loss of
OL,20,Fspecialist facilities and that it was
OL,21,F"pushing producers to fix the problem."
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
